  "gloss": "Muth-labben, white, brick",
  "summary": "Psalm 9 preserves a musical expression whose precise meaning is unknown. Its second word resembles several forms under this index. Elsewhere white describes animals, hair and branches, while brick and brickmaking appear together in the accounts of Babel and Egypt. Jacob cuts a fresh rod from this tree. Hosea describes people choosing its shade, along with that of the oak and terebinth, for their sacrifices.",
