  "doctrine": [],
  "note": "The heading is filed under its full wording. Its placement under לבנ follows the index and does not derive the musical phrase from white or brick. Reading death of the son requires separating the opening word. It may preserve a tune title, whose original setting is unknown. The tree לִבְנֶה already belongs to libneh.\n\nAdded 2026-11-21: לִבְנֶה, from its former one-word entry. Filed under לבנ 'be white' (the ־ה is the noun ending): Jewish Aramaic לְבָן is the white poplar and Arabic لُبْنَى the storax, named for its white bark or resin.\n\nIts former note: The Septuagint uses στυρακίνην, ‘of storax’, in Gen.30.37 and λεύκης, ‘of white poplar’, in Hos.4.13. Both renderings are aligned to this Hebrew noun in MACULA-LXX. The Ugaritic word occurs in a simile and its meaning is disputed."
